.TH "LINTO-INDEX" 1

.SH "Linto guide"
.PP
Linto is a local command\-line toolbox for bibliography work, Quarto projects,
text processing, and development helpers\. This guide is split into topic pages:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
\fBinstall\fP \-\- Installation and shell setup
.IP \(bu 4
\fBconfig\fP \-\- Group, Markdown\-viewer, and Zed configuration
.IP \(bu 4
\fBcommands\fP \-\- Commands and invocation, including shell alias setup
.IP \(bu 4
\fBbiblio\fP \-\- BibTeX and bibliography workflow
.IP \(bu 4
\fBquarto\fP \-\- Quarto workflow
.IP \(bu 4
\fBcompletion\fP \-\- Shell completion and Markdown navigation
.RE
.PP
Use \fBlinto help PAGE\fP to read a page in the terminal, for example \fBlinto help
config\fP\. If a page name is also an active group name, select it explicitly with
\fBlinto help page PAGE\fP (for example, \fBlinto help page bibtex\fP)\. \fBlinto help
GROUP\fP lists the group's current commands, and \fBlinto help GROUP COMMAND\fP shows
a command's help\.
.PP
Guide pages are rendered using the first installed program in the
\fBmarkdown\-viewer\fP preference list in \fBconfig\.yml\fP\. If none of the configured
viewers is installed, Linto displays the Markdown as plain text\. Set
\fBLINTO_MDVIEWER\fP to override the preference list for a single invocation\.
.PP
For a live list of active groups and commands, run \fBlinto \-\-help\fP\.
